## AIOS QEMU interleaved soak (text mode)

**Status:** finished (8 boots)

### Settings

| Setting | Value |
|---|---|
| Design | 2 arms (A, B), 4 rounds of one boot per arm: 8 boots |
| Rotation | the arm order moves by one each round: A B; B A, then again |
| Boots | 3s each, stall limit 2s, data disk fresh per boot |
| QEMU | QEMU emulator version 99.1.0 (aios test fake) (`<ROOT>/bin/qemu-system-aarch64`, sha256 `f6881a5e580c7942`) |
| Firmware | `<ROOT>/fw.fd` (sha256 `c3bf47ea1f4a4a60`) |
| Host | <HOST> |
| Load average | <L> |
| Load check | passed: load1 0.50 before the builds, not above the host's CPU count |
| Toolchains | one channel and one rustc for every arm |
| Arm base | every arm contains `244166f03dbd262e5ed2921769fb515ee7dd0652` (AIOS_SOAK_MIN_ARM_BASE override; the release base is `7167d408f6a43ca9859fb6238f608ca6bdee37d6`, #196) |
| Harness | <HARNESS> |
| Logs | `<ROOT>/repo/out` |

### Arms

| Arm | Checkout | Commit | Channel | rustc | Kernel |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A | `../arms/a` | `244166f` | nightly-2026-10-09 | rustc 1.99.0-nightly (fake 2026-10-09) | kernel ELF sha256 `94cc3f95c7b1a13c` |
| B | `../arms/b` | `244166f` | nightly-2026-10-09 | rustc 1.99.0-nightly (fake 2026-10-09) | kernel ELF sha256 `94cc3f95c7b1a13c` |

### Classes per arm

| Class | A | B |
|---|---:|---:|
| PCZERO | 0 | 0 |
| PANIC-LOCK | 0 | 0 |
| PANIC | 0 | 4 |
| EXCEPTION | 0 | 0 |
| WEDGE-STUCK | 0 | 0 |
| WEDGE-ALIVE | 0 | 0 |
| INCONCLUSIVE | 0 | 0 |
| DEGRADED | 0 | 0 |
| CLEAN | 4 | 0 |
| **Total** | 4 | 4 |
| CLEAN rate | 100% (95% Wilson interval 51%-100%) | 0% (95% Wilson interval 0%-49%) |

The CLEAN rate is over each arm's conclusive boots (INCONCLUSIVE left out).

### Load

The host's 1-minute load average before each boot.

| Arm | Boots with a load | load1 mean | load1 max |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| A | 4 | 0.50 | 0.50 |
| B | 4 | 0.50 | 0.50 |

A pair whose arms' mean loads differ by more than 25% of the lower mean is redone: the load, not the change, may explain its differences.

- A vs B: 0.50 vs 0.50, 0% apart: comparable

### Pair tests

Fisher's exact test on conclusive boots only (INCONCLUSIVE is left out of every count and denominator). In each pair the earlier arm is the previous one and the later arm the new one. The regression guard fails when the new arm has fewer CLEAN boots with one-sided p < 0.05. A class is marked `removed` when the new arm has none of it and the one-sided p (fewer in new) < 0.05, and `new` when the previous arm has none of it and the one-sided p (more in new) < 0.05. The rate differences (new - previous, in percentage points) are recorded, never gated on.

#### A vs B (A previous, B new)

**Regression guard:** CLEAN 4/4 in A, 0/4 in B; one-sided p (fewer CLEAN in B) = 0.0143: **fails** (p < 0.05)

| Class | A | B | B - A | p fewer in B | p more in B | p two-sided | Marker |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| PCZERO | 0/4 | 0/4 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| PANIC-LOCK | 0/4 | 0/4 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| PANIC | 0/4 | 4/4 | +100 pp | 1 | 0.0143 | 0.0286 | new |
| EXCEPTION | 0/4 | 0/4 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| WEDGE-STUCK | 0/4 | 0/4 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| WEDGE-ALIVE | 0/4 | 0/4 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| DEGRADED | 0/4 | 0/4 | 0 pp | 1 | 1 | 1 | - |
| CLEAN | 4/4 | 0/4 | -100 pp | 0.0143 | 1 | 0.0286 | removed |
| PANIC+PANIC-LOCK | 0/4 | 4/4 | +100 pp | 1 | 0.0143 | 0.0286 | new |

### Gate 1 IPC

| Arm | IPC round trip, mean over CLEAN boots | n | CLEAN boots without avg= | G1PASS boots |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| A | 6.00 us | 4 | 0 | 4 of 4 |
| B | n/a | 0 | 0 | 0 of 4 |

Each boot's avg= is whole us, as the kernel truncates it.

### Tripwire per arm

| Arm | Non-CLEAN boots with neither a complete tripwire line nor a fatal report |
|---|---:|
| A | 0 |
| B | n/a (no tripwire line in any boot) |

That count is meaningful only for an arm whose kernel prints tripwire lines (step 1b, e211d6d, or later); for an older arm every non-CLEAN boot without a fatal report counts.

From each boot's last complete `[tripwire]` line (the `tw_*` columns of `boots.tsv`), by arm. A cell is "boots with a non-zero value / sum over those boots", or "/ max" for a gauge (marked max). A per-CPU key's row without an index sums its CPUs. Values that are 0 in every boot are left out.

| Counter | A | B |
|---|---:|---:|
| Boots | 4 | 4 |
| Boots with a `v=1` line | 4 | 0 |
| `tick` | 4/4004 | 0/0 |
| `tick[CPU 0]` | 4/4004 | 0/0 |
| `elrmm` | 4/4 | 0/0 |
| `elrmm[CPU 0]` | 4/4 | 0/0 |
| `twc` | 4/36 | 0/0 |
| `twn` | 4/4 | 0/0 |
| `twmax` (max) | 4/94000 | 0/0 |

